      "categoryId": "visualization",
      "status": "learned",
      "summary": "A 3D point becomes a 2D pixel through model, view, perspective, and viewport transforms; depth is consumed during the perspective divide.",
      "what": "The 3D rendering pipeline normalizes axes, moves the scene relative to a camera, divides by depth, and maps normalized coordinates onto pixels.",
      "why": "It explains why 3D scatter plots can hide points, distort distances, and require rotation to resolve ambiguity.",
      "intuition": "A screen pixel is a ray into space: many different points can land on the same ray and look identical from one camera.",
      "how": ["Normalize data into world coordinates.", "Transform world coordinates into camera coordinates.", "Project x and y by dividing by depth.", "Map normalized coordinates to screen pixels and rotate to reveal collisions."],
      "visual": { "type":"flow", "title":"Three numbers become one pixel", "items":[{"label":"Data","detail":"(x, y, z)"},{"label":"World","detail":"normalize axes"},{"label":"Camera","detail":"lookAt transform"},{"label":"Projection","detail":"x/depth, y/depth"},{"label":"Pixel","detail":"2D screen"}] },
      "formula": { "expression":"screen x ∝ camera x / depth", "parts":[{"term":"camera x","meaning":"horizontal position relative to camera"},{"term":"depth","meaning":"distance in front of camera"},{"term":"divide","meaning":"far points shrink toward center"}], "example":"Iris row (5.1,3.5,1.4) maps to roughly pixel (403,354) in the worked camera." },
      "code": "ndc_x = (focal / aspect) * camera_x / depth\nndc_y = focal * camera_y / depth",
      "example": "Two Iris flowers 1.33 cm apart in data land only 0.77 pixels apart from the default camera.",
      "confusions": ["3D distance on screen is not distance in the raw data.", "Orthographic projection removes perspective shrinking but not occlusion.", "A static screenshot removes the rotation cue that makes 3D useful."],
      "prerequisites": ["numpy-math-linear-algebra", "plotly-interactive-charts"], "related": ["iris-eda"],
